Excellent. Part V is actually one of the most important parts of the entire PCS specification.

Up until now, we have designed how cognition exists.

But a real cognitive system cannot only store and retrieve knowledge.

It must also be:

trustworthy,
recoverable,
auditable,
secure,
resilient against failures,
able to explain itself.

