Important new concept introduced: Cognitive Recovery Objective (CRO)

I think this is a genuinely important MOS-specific idea.

Traditional systems ask:

"Did the database recover?"

MOS asks:

"Did the intelligence recover?"

A recovered system should not only have files and tables.

It should recover:

knowledge,
reasoning capability,
learned skills,
historical understanding,
decision context.

This gives MOS a new operational metric:

Cognitive Availability

Not:

"Is the server online?"

But:

"Can the system still think correctly?"
